       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). That is about twice the maximum.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is also well above the typical maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n\nAt this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total daily, such as 850 mg twice daily\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose you intended. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
